        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0000105</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>The main causes of large kidney are hydronephrosis, polycystic disease, renal cell carcinoma, nephroblastoma/Wilms tumor (in children), and solitary cysts. If possible, a specific term should be used instead of this one. There are several ways of diagnosing enlarged kidney including intravenous urography.</rdfs:comment>
