        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0000520</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/hp#hposlim_core"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Some sources define &quot;exophthalmos&quot; as a protrusion of the globe greater than 18 mm and &quot;proptosis&quot; as a protusion equal to or less than 18 mm. Others define &quot;exophthalmos&quot; as protusion secondary to endocrine dysfunction and &quot;proptosis&quot; as any non-endocrine-mediated protusion (Source: Wikipedia). This finding should be distinguished frm underdevelopment of the supraorbital ridge or maxilla/zygoma. In proptosis, the globe is anteriorly protuberant to the overall plane of the face.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Proptosis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
