        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Loss of words</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0002381</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Aphasia is caused by brain injury. The most common cause is stroke, but aphasia can also be caused by other factors such as head trauma, brain tumors, or infections. The terms aphasia and dysphasia are usually considered to be synonymous, but the word dysphasia has been used inconsistently and it is recommended to no longer use the term dysphasia.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Aphasia</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
