        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/hp#hposlim_core"/>
        <rdfs:comment>The foramen magnum is the aperture through which the medulla oblongata enters and exits the skull. Stenosis of the foramen magnum can represent a risk for compression to the spinal cord.</rdfs:comment>
