        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0004371</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>A glycosaminoglycan is any polysaccharide containing a substantial proportion of aminomonosaccharide residues. Glycosaminoglycan (GAG) are long unbranched polysaccharides consisting of a repeating disaccharide unit. Among the most common GAGs are chondroitin sulfate, dermatan sulfate, chondroitin sulfate, keratan sulfate, heparan sulfate, and hyaluronan.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Abnormality of glycosaminoglycan metabolism</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
