        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Dilated heart right ventricle</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0005133</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Ventricular dilatation is to be distinguished from ventricular aneurysm, which refers to a diastolic as well as systolic outpouching of the ventricle containing endocardium, epicardium, and thin-wall non-contractile scarred myocardium, which mainly develop in the setting of a full-thickness infarct, replaced by fibrous tissue because of myocardial infarction.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Right ventricular dilatation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0005133"/>
