        <obo:IAO_0000115>Pseudarthrosis, or &quot;false joint&quot; of the tibia is the result of a developmental failure in the tibia progressing to spontaneous fracture and subsequent fibrous nonunion. The fracture is rarely present at birth but commonly develops during the first 18 months of life.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199"/>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2009-01-31T11:22:24Z</terms:date>
