        <rdfs:comment>Principal causative agents include herpes simplex virus (HSV), which causes recurrent herpetic stomatitis particularly in T-cell deficiencies, and Coxsackievirus (hand-foot-and-mouth disease), which may be unusually severe or prolonged in antibody deficiencies.</rdfs:comment>
