        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Abnormality of temperature sensation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Impaired temperature sensation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Impaired thermal sensitivity</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Loss of temperature sensation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0010829</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Temperature sensation can be tested by touching the skin several seconds with a water flask filled to the desired temperature. Persons with normal temperature sensation should at least be able to identify as warm a flask that is 35-36 degrees C and identify as cool a flask at 28-32 degrees C.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Impaired temperature sensation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
