        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025668"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0034058"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Nuchal translucency is the sonographic appearance of subcutaneous accumulation of liquid in the back of the fetal neck in the first trimester of pregnancy (11-14 gestational weeks of pregnancy).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199"/>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2010-09-13T08:15:19Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C4023676</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0010880</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Increased nuchal translucency may be related to a cystic hygroma or to mesenchymal edema. Increased nuchal translucency can be classified into three categories: 1) cardiac abnormalities, combined with abnormal ductus venosus flow velocities, is found, leading to the theory that cardiac failure causes nuchal translucency enlargement; 2) various types of abnormalities are found in the extracellular matrix of the nuchal skin of fetuses with increased nuchal translucency; 3) abnormal lymphatic development is demonstrated in fetuses with increased nuchal translucency.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Increased nuchal translucency</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010880"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Nuchal translucency is the sonographic appearance of subcutaneous accumulation of liquid in the back of the fetal neck in the first trimester of pregnancy (11-14 gestational weeks of pregnancy).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:12751779</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:15846173</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28511453</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


