        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0003117"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An abnormal concentration of corticotropin in the blood.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:creator rdf:resource="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0736-9199"/>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2011-03-10T07:46:59Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C4023574</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Abnormality of circulating corticotropin level</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Abnormality of circulating ACTH level</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Abnormality of circulating adrenocorticotropic hormone level</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Abnormality of circulating adrenocorticotropin level</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0011043</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH), also known as corticotropin, is a polypeptide hormone produced and secreted by the pituitary gland comprising 39 amino acid residues coupled in a linear sequence. . It is a component of the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis and stimulates increased production and release of corticosteroids and cortisol from the adrenal cortex.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Abnormal circulating adrenocorticotropin concentration</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0011043"/>
