        <oboInOwl:id>HP:0012025</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:comment>Ornithine is an amino acid produced in the urea cycle by the splitting off of urea from arginine. Ornithine is a naturally occurring, non-proteinogenic amino acid found in meat, fish, dairy and eggs.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Abnormal circulating ornithine concentration</rdfs:label>
