        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Reduced thyroxine-binding globulin level</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Reduced thyroxine-binding globulin level in blood</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Thyroxine-binding globulin low in blood</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Thyroxin-binding globulin (TBG) is known as serpin peptidase inhibitor, clade A (alpha-1 antiproteinase, antitrypsin), member 7 (SERPINA7), Entrez Gene ID 6906. Individuals with TBG deficiency are euthyroid. TBG is responsible for carrying the thyroid hormones thyroxine (T4) and 3,5,3&apos;-triiodothyronine (T3) in the bloodstream.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Decreased circulating thyroxine-binding globulin concentration</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


