        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0010990"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Deficiency of factor XIII subunit A, leading to a reduced factor XIII activity. Activated Factor XIII cross-links fibrin polymers solidifying the clot.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2016-01-21T17:03:48Z</terms:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C2750514</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Reduced factor XIII, subunit A</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Measurement of subunit A or B can be performed by Elisa kits. Adding the more granular term would facilitate mutation analysis as both subunits are encoded by different genes. This is not always performed in the diagnostic workup so &apos;Reduced factor XIII activity&apos; would sufice. This term has been requested and created by members of the BRIDGE consortium</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Factor XIII subunit A deficiency</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


