        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0410008"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any abnormality of the part of the peripheral nervous system associated with sensation and skeletal muscle voluntary control of body movements.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C4073188</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SoNS consists of afferent and efferent nerves. Afferent nerves are responsible for relaying sensation to the central nervous system; efferent nerves are responsible for stimulating muscle contraction, including all the non-sensory neurons connected with skeletal muscles and skin.</rdfs:comment>
