        <terms:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2017-04-24T15:34:43Z</terms:date>
        <rdfs:comment>Urethritis is characterized by discharge, dysuria and/or urethral discomfort but may be asymptomatic. Common etiologies include gonococcal urethritis as well as infection by chlamydia trachomatis, mycoplasma genitalium, ureaplasma urealyticum, trichomonas vaginalis, anaerobes, herpes simplex virus, and adenovirus.</rdfs:comment>
